It seems to me that Tibor Machan's analysis (quoted by Mark Venture on
Friday, in digest 103) ignores time.

Suppose Alice creates a machine and gives it to Bob; Bob gives it to Cathy;
Bob dies (or otherwise ceases to be a moral agent); Cathy gives the machine
to me.  (For "gives" read "sells" if you prefer; it makes no difference.)

